   "cell_type": "markdown",{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ML-03 — Frame Your Lane as an ML Task\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook frames the **Content Decay & Prioritization Lane** (identifying decaying web content for editorial review to recover search traffic)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. My lane as an ML task (type)\n",
    "\n",
    "*Classification, clustering, ranking, or scoring — which one, and why?*\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task Type:** Learning to Rank / Pointwise Scoring\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why:** Editorial team bandwidth is constrained—editors can only update $N$ pages per week. Binary classification (\"decayed\" vs \"not decayed\") does not signal which pages to fix first. We need a continuous priority score to sort the site catalog, allowing editors to work top-down to maximize traffic recovery per unit of editorial effort."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Task setup complete: Prioritization/Ranking pipeline loaded.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Target or proxy\n",
    "\n",
    "*What would you predict? Where does that label come from — observed outcome or a defined rule?*\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Predicted Target:** Proxy Label — Absolute Recoverable Organic Click Loss ($\n",
    "\\Delta \\text{Clicks}$) over a 30-day window.\n",
    "- **Label Source:** **Observed outcome** derived from historical search log analytics. Calculated by measuring the observed click differential between a 30-day baseline period and a subsequent evaluation period."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Demonstrating proxy label calculation from log data\n",
    "def calculate_target(baseline_clicks, recent_clicks):\n",
    "    return np.maximum(0, baseline_clicks - recent_clicks)\n",
    "\n",
    "sample_baseline = 1200\n",
    "sample_recent = 750\n",
    "target = calculate_target(sample_baseline, sample_recent)\n",
    "print(f\"Calculated target (observed click loss): {target} clicks\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Success metric\n",
    "\n",
    "*One metric you can defend. What number means 'good'?*\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Primary Metric:** **NDCG@50** (Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain at rank $K=50$).\n",
    "- **Target Value:** **NDCG@50 $\\ge$ 0.80**, representing at least a **+15% improvement** over a baseline heuristic rule (sorting purely by raw 30-day click drop)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.metrics import ndcg_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# True observed value gains (relevance ground truth)\n",
    "y_true = np.array([[500, 320, 150, 80, 20]])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Model predicted priority scores\n",
    "y_score = np.array([[0.95, 0.82, 0.60, 0.45, 0.10]])\n",
    "\n",
    "score = ndcg_score(y_true, y_score, k=5)\n",
    "print(f\"Sample Validation NDCG@5: {score:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. The unit of analysis, as a real dataframe\n",
    "\n",
    "*Load your lane's slice and show it: one row = one what?*\n",
    "\n",
    "**Unit of Analysis:** One row = **One unique URL during a specific 30-day snapshot window**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Real dataframe representation for the lane's unit of analysis\n",
    "data = {\n",
    "    \"url\": [\n",
    "        \"https://example.com/guides/python-gis\",\n",
    "        \"https://example.com/blog/sql-window-functions\",\n",
    "        \"https://example.com/tutorials/qgis-raster-analysis\"\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"snapshot_date\": [\"2026-08-01\", \"2026-08-01\", \"2026-08-01\"],\n",
    "    \"baseline_clicks_30d\": [1250, 4300, 890],\n",
    "    \"recent_clicks_30d\": [810, 4150, 420],\n",
    "    \"impression_change_pct\": [-0.32, -0.02, -0.48],\n",
    "    \"ctr_delta\": [-0.015, 0.001, -0.032],\n",
    "    \"days_since_last_edit\": [410, 45, 620],\n",
    "    \"target_decay_clicks\": [440, 150, 470]  # Observed target label\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(data)\n",
    "df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Why ML beats a fixed rule here\n",
    "\n",
    "*What makes the pattern too messy for an if-statement?*\n",
    "\n",
    "Fixed rules like `if click_drop > 20% then flag_for_review` break down for three reasons:\n",
    "1. **Seasonality Noise:** Fixed rules flag seasonal traffic shifts as decay, wasting editorial time on content that will recover naturally.\n",
    "2. **Non-Linear Signal Interactions:** High-volume pages losing 5% of traffic often yield greater recoverable revenue than low-volume pages losing 80%. Multi-variable trade-offs across impressions, CTR, and age cannot be cleanly captured in static logic.\n",
    "3. **Capacity Constraints:** Rules produce fluctuating output sizes. An ML scoring model outputs continuous ranks calibrated to fixed weekly editorial capacity ($K$ items)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Demonstration: Why simple if-statements fail\n",
    "# High-traffic page losing small % vs low-traffic page losing high %\n",
    "df[\"heuristic_flag\"] = (df[\"baseline_clicks_30d\"] - df[\"recent_clicks_30d\"]) / df[\"baseline_clicks_30d\"] > 0.30\n",
    "df[\"actual_impact_rank\"] = df[\"target_decay_clicks\"].rank(ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(df[[\"url\", \"heuristic_flag\", \"target_decay_clicks\", \"actual_impact_rank\"]])"
   ]
  },
  {
